  "targetCommit": {
    "sha": "72fb194ffc79337a0c8f65591c9579f40be06ce2",
    "url": "https://github.com/DoctorFlux/FluxUI/commit/72fb194ffc79337a0c8f65591c9579f40be06ce2",
    "message": "Improve combat-safe startup and reduce idle UI work\n\nInitialize secure infrastructure at the earliest legal lifecycle phase,\nretain native controls until replacements are usable, and reconcile queued\nstructural work after combat. Preserve the Forever VARIABLES_LOADED barrier.\n\nProtect customized bindings and respec recovery checkpoints, replace global\nBaganator item overrides with local adapters, and preserve legacy settings\nthrough validated reversible migrations. Make module initialization retryable.\n\nReuse Flux Window content, cancel stale callbacks, defer nonessential startup,\nand reduce redundant bar, unit-frame, stats, map and HUD refresh work. Coalesce\nbag-counter callbacks and avoid unchanged character-button layout writes.\nExtend opt-in startup and idle diagnostics without permanent profiling work.\n\nInclude production-backed regression fixtures, source manifests and measured\noperation counts. Retained baseline fixtures preserve original whitespace.\n\nValidation: 51/51 desktop Lua checks pass; 688 Lua files pass syntax checks.\nDocumentation inventory and 12,231 local links pass validation. Native\nfive-client combat acceptance remains pending, and the remaining Forever\nidle FPS gap is documented as unresolved."
  },
